            0.108,
            0.883,
            0.149
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Observe that the amount left on the "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "n ^ { t h }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " day will be `(100 – 5n). Therefore, on the 12th day the amount left will be "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "(100 - 12 \\times 5) = 540"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.164,
            0.399,
            0.188
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Think and Reflect"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.201,
            0.867,
            0.241
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What amount will be left on the 15th day? How many days will it take for the entire amount to be spent?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.258,
            0.885,
            0.315
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 8:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " An auto-rikshaw fare starts at `25 and remains the same for the initial 2 km. Then it increases by `15 per km. What will be the fare for a travel of 10 km?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.315,
            0.885,
            0.375
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "For the initial 2 km, the fare is `25. For every kilometre (km) thereafter, the fare will increase by `15. Therefore, the total fare for a travel of 10 km will be "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "25+15\\times8=7145"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.382,
            0.88,
            0.457
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "table_body",
              "index": 7,
              "bbox": [
                0.116,
                0.382,
                0.88,
                0.457
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_7_table_7.jpg",
              "content": "<table><tbody><tr><td>Km travelled</td><td>1</td><td>2</td><td>3</td><td>4</td><td>5</td><td>6</td></tr><tr><td>Fare (`)</td><td>25</td><td>25</td><td>25 + 1 × 15= 40</td><td>25 + 2 × 15= 55</td><td>25 + 3 × 15= 70</td><td>25 + 4 × 15= 85</td></tr></tbody></table>"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.466,
            0.885,
            0.526
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Observe that the total fare for a travel of n km will be "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "25+15\\times(n-2)=15n-5"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " when "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "n \\geq 2"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Here, the fare for a specific distance covered is a function of the distance n km."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.55,
            0.399,
            0.574
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Think and Reflect"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.13,
            0.587,
            0.531,
            0.608
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "For how many km will the fare be `130?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.639,
            0.886,
            0.721
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Note that in all the above examples, the "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "n ^ { t h }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " term is a linear expression in n. A "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "linear pattern",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is a sequence of numbers where the difference between two consecutive terms is constant. We will learn more about linear patterns in the chapter on Sequences and Progressions."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.375,
            0.742,
            0.622,
            0.771
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Exercise Set 2.3"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.79,
            0.334,
            0.811
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Solve the following:"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.814,
            0.886,
            0.899
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. A student has `500 in her savings bank account. She gets `150 every month as pocket money. How much money will she have at the end of every month from the second month onwards? Find a linear expression to represent the amount she will have in the "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "n ^ { t h }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " month."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
